<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sremski Karlovci</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Karlowitz, Karlovci</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sremski Karlovci is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrmia">Syrmia</a>, now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> was signed there in 1699, and it became the seat of the Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> metropolitans in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg Monarchy</a>. In May 1848 the May Assembly held there proclaimed the Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vojvodina">Vojvodina</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sremski-karlovci.jpg" alt="Sremski Karlovci" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ванилица · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vidikovac_Sremski_Karlovci_8295_10.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
